## Key takeaways (in my own words)
- **AI augments, it doesn't replace** — human oversight keeps outputs accurate, fair and within legal limits.
- **Prompting:** I use the **TCREI** framework (Task, Context, References, Evaluate, Iterate) for every prompt.
- **Responsible AI:** five types of harm — allocative, quality-of-service, representational,
  social system and interpersonal — and bias comes largely from skewed training data.
- **Three terms not to mix up:** context window, knowledge cutoff and drift.
- **Privacy:** never enter real personal data — use placeholders (data minimisation).
- **AI security:** models can be attacked through data poisoning, prompt injection,
  malicious model files, adversarial examples and jailbreaking.

